  "production_date": "1616-18",
  "brief_description": "Three men, one with a crown, stand in a landscape. They hold between them a large piece of paper, while two are pointing to a classical city in the background. The gods Apollo and Neptune have disguised themselves as mortals to advise King Laomedon on the building of Troy.\n\nThis is one of ten frescoes designed by Domenichino, painted with the help of assistants, to decorate a magnificent garden pavilion at the Villa Aldobrandini in Frascati, near Rome. Many of the scenes, including this one, were taken from the Roman poet Ovid's Metamorphoses. Eight of them were transferred to canvas and are now in our collection.",
